0..74 Comment "// A theory\'s terms where its rules present no type, or where the slice of"
75..103 Comment "// theories with terms ends."
104..106 Comment "//"
107..179 Comment "// `Terms(S)` is the data type of a theory\'s closed terms, its rules the"
180..257 Comment "// type\'s conversion. A monoid\'s associativity orients to no decreasing rule,"
258..335 Comment "// so its terms have no presentation. A theory of two sorts, or one stating a"
336..369 Comment "// law, stands outside the slice."
370..372 Comment "//"
373..445 Comment "// The refusal stands at the type that asks for the terms. A declaration"
446..524 Comment "// refused at refused terms states the terms\' own cause, never the consequence"
525..548 Comment "// that no data formed."
549..551 Comment "//"
552..622 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/theory-terms.gandr` — the unital magma\'s terms"
623..684 Comment "// - see: #4150 — not implemented: terms over several sorts"
685..757 Comment "// - see: #4105 — not implemented: a stated law as a cell of the terms"
